{"id": "EUVD-2026-108729", "enisaUuid": "72aa855d-070d-30e4-8ee9-1d4d24879d86", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm ioctl: don't let data_start run past the buffer\n\nstruct dm_ioctl has seven bytes of trailing padding, so the smallest\nbuffer userspace is allowed to ask for, offsetof(struct dm_ioctl, data),\nis seven bytes shorter than sizeof(struct dm_ioctl).\n\nget_result_buffer() sets data_start to sizeof(struct dm_ioctl) without\nlooking at how big the buffer actually is. Ask for the minimum and\ndata_start ends up seven bytes past the end. Callers add it to\ndata_size, and ctl_ioctl() copies that much back to userspace:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in _copy_to_user+0xad/0xd0\n  Read of size 312 at addr ffff8880169e4c00 by task repro-dm/140\n   ctl_ioctl+0x5e3/0xcb0\n   dm_ctl_ioctl+0x25/0x40\n  allocated 305-byte region [ffff8880169e4c00, ffff8880169e4d31)\n\nA DM_LIST_DEVICES with data_size set to 305 is enough to hit it, and the\nseven bytes that leak are whatever sat next to the allocation.\n\nClamp data_start to the buffer size.\n\nNote that this is not a security bug because the out-of-bounds read can\nonly be triggered by root.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:23:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:23:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/98195e822343a656b92e235847ab3e72b1a3f920", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e5c3f3d8935ecc64c962fb66e6a86dbf79218f61", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5680b6fb3054677d4ee65d3baba24b649f1b430e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/725b49c689bbb29ef740b0d6b5ea9390baa9a695", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b3fcf519d370df94a56f3b272d9eddffffa5be8"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99063"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1f61aac2-2d23-39a0-a562-d5b50f507b96", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "2ce8b2ae-09f1-34f6-b63e-19fa474d6a45", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "76c072b48e39e9291fbf02d6c912cf27d65e093d <9b3fcf519d370df94a56f3b272d9eddffffa5be8"}, {"id": "2e1ad48a-362b-3808-b303-33e3babfda1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "35f2f43b-41f6-3f50-b170-ace56abc575a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "76c072b48e39e9291fbf02d6c912cf27d65e093d <725b49c689bbb29ef740b0d6b5ea9390baa9a695"}, {"id": "7edd49cc-d36b-3031-bac2-ee4ceaff59e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "76c072b48e39e9291fbf02d6c912cf27d65e093d <5680b6fb3054677d4ee65d3baba24b649f1b430e"}, {"id": "981af75b-d116-3da4-9ca3-a16aee2d6a9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "a7018b0f-4d32-32bc-843d-80bae75805c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "76c072b48e39e9291fbf02d6c912cf27d65e093d <e5c3f3d8935ecc64c962fb66e6a86dbf79218f61"}, {"id": "b8680f25-d622-366c-a255-0d2ab34aeb65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "76c072b48e39e9291fbf02d6c912cf27d65e093d <98195e822343a656b92e235847ab3e72b1a3f920"}, {"id": "be05e37a-ca6f-3911-842d-de7deb3ad2eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "d75d0997-2e38-3ff9-9beb-798ff3cdd5f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d8aaa914-5014-3ed5-b366-39aadb393627", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "e1ec466a-acaa-38e2-a996-cb7b77a62e38", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.25"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "21402a61-bd0a-3c7e-abbb-7f53c1dbf7b8", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}